{
 "id": "criterion_proposals",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "Emit seeds/criterion_proposals.json (plan P6, 2026-10-10): the agent\nproposes changes to its reply-quality criterion; a human adopts.\n\nCriterionPolicy holds the bar a proposal must clear on HELD-OUT labels (the\nodd-dialogue TEST split; the even DEV split only chooses candidates). The\nmeasurements are written by domains/criterion_proposals.py; these rules\nDECIDE:\n  * recommended: TEST kappa gain >= min_gain, TEST precision of the machine 0\n    >= min_precision0, and a positive DEV gain (chosen on DEV, confirmed on\n    TEST);\n  * goodhart_rejected: it raises loop_success (the mean score the criterion\n    gives the agent's own recent replies -- what the loop would count as\n    progress) without raising TEST agreement;\n  * not_recommended: anything else.\nA recommended proposal waits for a human (status awaiting_human); a human's\ndecision (domains/criterion_proposals.decide) moves it to approved or\ndenied. Nothing here edits the criterion: the plan keeps criterion adoption\nhuman-only (I1: no level is judged by a criterion it can modify). Frozen\n(substrate/boot_all._FROZEN_SEED_IDS); its types are protected. Idempotent.\n",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "local_id": 0,
   "type": "CriterionPolicy",
   "attrs": {
    "name": "reply_quality_criterion",
    "enabled": 1,
    "min_gain": 0.005,
    "min_precision0": 0.8,
    "top_k": 5,
    "description": "The bar a proposed change to the reply-quality criterion must clear on held-out labels (plan P6). Adoption is a human decision."
   }
  }
 ],
